  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nLow pressure will weaken across California for Friday and Saturday\nwith weak low pressure off the California coast on Saturday moving\ninto central and southern California on Sunday and Monday with\nlimited moisture. High temperatures will warm a few degrees for\nFriday and Saturday, then cool a few degrees for Sunday and\nMonday.\n\nHigh temperatures on Saturday will be a few degrees above average\nfor lower deserts and a few degrees below average for most other\nareas with high temperatures ranging from the 70s near the coast\nto the mid 80s to lower 90s for the Inland Empire with 100 to 104\nfor the lower deserts. With the cooling, high temperatures on \nMonday will range from the lower to mid 70s near the coast to the \n80s for the Inland Empire with the lower deserts around 100.\n\nFor the middle and latter part of next week, high pressure to the\neast is expected to strengthen, bringing a warming trend to \nsouthwestern California for Tuesday through Friday, though with \nincreasing uncertainty and model spread in just how much warming \nmay occur. The NBM 50th percentile high temperatures for Wednesday\nof next week are within a few degrees of average for most \nlocations.",
